WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:05.560
So what is standalone CTE?

00:05.840 --> 00:10.920
It is a city query that is defined and used independently in the query.

00:11.120 --> 00:14.840
So this means it is self-contained and it doesn't depend on anything.

00:14.840 --> 00:18.520
It doesn't depend on any other CTE or queries.

00:18.560 --> 00:24.240
So that means we can run the standalone query independently from anything inside our query.

00:24.280 --> 00:25.840
So let's understand what this means.

00:25.880 --> 00:26.840
We have our CTE.

00:26.920 --> 00:29.920
It's going to go and query the database tables.

00:29.920 --> 00:32.600
And in the output we will get an intermediate results.

00:32.600 --> 00:35.640
And then the output can be used from the main query.

00:35.680 --> 00:40.600
So the main query and query the intermediate results and present in the output the final results.

00:40.640 --> 00:44.920
So now if you check our CTE it is completely independent from anything else.

00:45.040 --> 00:47.040
So it's simply query the database.

00:47.040 --> 00:48.840
And it has one output.

00:48.880 --> 00:54.600
So since this CTE is independent from anything else we call it a standalone CTE.

00:54.640 --> 00:59.520
Now if you compare this city with the main query, you can see that the main query cannot be executed

00:59.520 --> 01:00.160
alone.

01:00.160 --> 01:03.680
And that's because it needs the result from the first query.

01:03.800 --> 01:08.660
So we cannot say the main query is independent, cannot be executed alone.

01:08.660 --> 01:11.340
It always depends on the city query.

01:11.340 --> 01:14.220
So this means that he first need to be executed.

01:14.260 --> 01:16.420
Then the main query can be executed.

01:16.420 --> 01:19.180
So this is what we mean with the standalone city.

01:19.460 --> 01:21.740
It doesn't depend on anything else.

01:21.780 --> 01:24.060
So now we can understand the syntax of the city.

01:24.100 --> 01:27.180
So we have a very simple query select from where.

01:27.220 --> 01:29.860
So it is a very simple Select statements.

01:29.900 --> 01:35.220
Now in order to put it inside a CTE we can go and use the With clause.

01:35.220 --> 01:39.140
So it starts with the keyword with then the CTE name.

01:39.140 --> 01:40.540
It's like a table name.

01:40.540 --> 01:46.420
And then we have the keyword as in in order to say this CTE is defined like the following.

01:46.540 --> 01:48.780
So this is the definition of the CTE.

01:48.820 --> 01:52.060
And it has two parenthesis the starting and the ending.

01:52.060 --> 01:57.020
So with this you are telling SQL okay now we are talking about CTE and it has a name.

01:57.020 --> 02:01.700
So if you are using a query inside a With clause we call this a CTE query.

02:01.860 --> 02:04.180
It is where you define the CTE.

02:04.460 --> 02:06.740
Now of course we don't want only to define a CTE.

02:06.780 --> 02:07.860
We want to use it.

02:07.860 --> 02:11.630
So outside of this definition we can go and use it like this.

02:11.630 --> 02:15.470
So we are saying select from the city name.

02:15.470 --> 02:19.110
So that means we want to select the data from the result of the CTE.

02:19.190 --> 02:24.710
And here it's very important to use exactly the same name as you define it in the With clause.

02:24.710 --> 02:28.550
So if you leave it like this we can call this the main query.

02:28.590 --> 02:31.510
It is the place where we use the CTE.

02:31.750 --> 02:35.990
So this is the syntax of a very simple CTE in SQL okay.

02:36.030 --> 02:40.470
So now what we're going to do we're going to have like a task that's going to keep progressing through

02:40.470 --> 02:41.230
this section.

02:41.230 --> 02:42.710
So we're going to start with the first tab.

02:42.710 --> 02:45.910
And we will keep adding steps as we progress in the CTE.

02:45.950 --> 02:51.030
So now the first step in this task says find the total sales per customer.

02:51.070 --> 02:54.870
And now of course since we have only one step, it makes no sense to use the CTE.

02:55.070 --> 02:59.510
But we will use it since we know that there will be different steps later.

02:59.510 --> 03:01.110
So let's start doing that now.

03:01.110 --> 03:04.870
Before I use any CTE, I would like just to write our query first.

03:04.870 --> 03:08.230
So we need the total sales for each customers is very simple.

03:08.230 --> 03:09.790
So we're going to go and select.

03:09.790 --> 03:10.670
And what do we need.

03:10.670 --> 03:16.650
Let's go and get the customer ID and we need to do aggregations on their sales.

03:16.650 --> 03:18.930
So summarize the sales.

03:18.930 --> 03:23.570
And we're going to call it total sales from the table.

03:23.610 --> 03:28.090
And now since this is our first query, we have to get the data from our database.

03:28.090 --> 03:29.490
So we don't have any other option.

03:29.530 --> 03:31.930
Our data are going to be in the sales orders.

03:31.930 --> 03:33.810
So let's go and get it.

03:33.810 --> 03:36.690
And don't forget to group by for the aggregation.

03:36.690 --> 03:38.850
We are grouping by the customer ID.

03:39.050 --> 03:39.730
That's it.

03:39.770 --> 03:41.450
Let's go and execute it.

03:41.450 --> 03:43.570
And as you can see in the output, nothing is fancy.

03:43.570 --> 03:46.170
We are just aggregating the sales by the customers.

03:46.170 --> 03:47.890
So with that we have solved the task.

03:47.890 --> 03:50.810
But now I would like to put my query in a CTE.

03:51.130 --> 03:53.410
And that's because later we're going to add more steps.

03:53.410 --> 03:56.210
So let's put our query in CTE.

03:56.330 --> 04:00.290
And in order to do that we're going to start with the with keyword.

04:00.330 --> 04:02.770
And now we have to define the name of the CTE.

04:02.770 --> 04:07.610
So I'm going to call it city underscore total sales like this.

04:07.610 --> 04:13.010
And then afterwards we're going to say as and then we have to go and add the parentheses at the start.

04:13.010 --> 04:14.850
And as well at the end.

04:14.850 --> 04:19.010
And with that we are telling SQL this query is a CTE query.

04:19.010 --> 04:26.660
So this means the SQL should store the result of this query in a cache in memory to be used later in

04:26.660 --> 04:27.620
the main query.

04:27.660 --> 04:33.500
Our CTE and of course what is missing is the main query, and you have to do it exactly after the definition

04:33.500 --> 04:34.260
of the CTE.

04:34.380 --> 04:37.700
I will just make here a small comment about the main query.

04:37.740 --> 04:40.580
And let me just make this smaller like this.

04:40.620 --> 04:45.340
And now we have to go and have a very simple select statements from.

04:45.380 --> 04:48.460
And now I would like to get more details from the customers table.

04:48.460 --> 04:51.180
So I will just go now to the customers.

04:53.380 --> 04:55.900
So now we are not querying the CTE right.

04:55.900 --> 04:58.700
We are just querying the database table that we have.

04:58.740 --> 05:06.820
And I would like to get from the customer, the customer ID and the first name and let's go and get

05:06.820 --> 05:08.420
as well the last name.

05:09.580 --> 05:13.220
So now if we go and query this, what happens in the output?

05:13.220 --> 05:18.860
We are getting the data actually completely from the database table, the customers.

05:18.860 --> 05:24.180
And of course we are not using at all the CTE inside our main query because we can do that, but it's

05:24.180 --> 05:29.880
just waste of space in the memory because SQL did execute this and stored it in the.

05:29.920 --> 05:30.800
Database memory.

05:30.800 --> 05:33.960
And of course we would like to use the CTE in our main query.

05:33.960 --> 05:35.280
So let's go and do that.

05:35.640 --> 05:37.320
So let's go and do a join.

05:37.880 --> 05:41.040
But this time we're going to join the data from the CTE.

05:41.440 --> 05:43.160
So let's go and get the name.

05:43.560 --> 05:45.880
And I will just call it CTS.

05:46.000 --> 05:51.960
So what we are doing now we are joining the physical table, the customers with the virtual table that

05:51.960 --> 05:56.640
you have created with the CTE that exist only in our query.

05:56.680 --> 06:01.760
And of course, not only we are joining the tables, we would like to get the informations from the

06:01.760 --> 06:02.200
CTE.

06:02.240 --> 06:05.760
So CTS and we need only that total sales.

06:05.760 --> 06:07.880
So total sales.

06:08.560 --> 06:13.200
So that means those three columns comes from our database table customers.

06:13.200 --> 06:14.360
And only this column.

06:14.360 --> 06:16.520
The total sales comes from our CTE.

06:16.560 --> 06:18.560
So let's go and execute the whole thing.

06:18.680 --> 06:21.000
Now as you can see in the output everything is working.

06:21.160 --> 06:24.160
We have the three columns from the table customers.

06:24.160 --> 06:26.880
And we have the total sales for each customer.

06:26.880 --> 06:29.200
And this total sales comes from our CTE.

06:29.280 --> 06:32.900
Now as you can see the last customer has a null over here.

06:32.900 --> 06:36.860
And that's because in the table orders we don't have the customer five.

06:36.900 --> 06:40.980
And now you might say, you know what, I would like to see the intermediate result from the CTE.

06:41.140 --> 06:46.140
Because what you are seeing now in the output is the final result from the main query.

06:46.260 --> 06:52.300
So now what we can do in order to see the result of the CTE, we're going to mark the query in the CTE

06:52.500 --> 06:56.980
course without any parentheses or the with so just the query and execute it.

06:56.980 --> 07:02.540
And with that you can see in the output the intermediate results that we are passing to the main query.

07:02.900 --> 07:05.540
And as you can see we don't have here customer number five.

07:05.660 --> 07:09.060
That's why in the final results we are getting null.

07:09.060 --> 07:11.900
And that's of course because we are using the left join.

07:11.900 --> 07:16.660
So if I execute the whole thing you can see we are getting the customer five over here with the null.

07:16.660 --> 07:18.340
So as you can see CTE is very simple.

07:18.340 --> 07:21.300
We just treat it as any normal database table.

07:21.300 --> 07:26.380
But this table is created from our query that we have defined in the CTE over here.

07:26.420 --> 07:33.220
Now of course in the CTE you can use any kind of clauses like select from join group by having everything

07:33.220 --> 07:38.950
that you want window functions all aggregate functions, but there is only one restriction.

07:38.950 --> 07:44.910
You cannot go and use the order by clause, so you cannot sort the data in the CTE.

07:44.950 --> 07:46.710
So let's go and try it out.

07:47.030 --> 07:49.110
Let's go and say order by.

07:49.270 --> 07:52.510
And let's say I want to sort by the order ID for example.

07:52.670 --> 07:54.430
So let's go and execute it.

07:54.430 --> 08:00.830
You can see here SQL is saying okay I cannot do it for you because order by is not allowed in many things.

08:00.830 --> 08:05.470
So you cannot use it in views in subqueries in common table expressions.

08:05.470 --> 08:06.830
The CTE over here.

08:06.990 --> 08:08.190
So it is not allowed.

08:08.190 --> 08:10.510
You cannot use order by in the CTE.

08:10.550 --> 08:14.430
But of course you can go and sort the data in the main query.

08:14.430 --> 08:23.190
So if you go over here and say order by customer ID, so if we execute it it's going to be working.

08:23.190 --> 08:25.390
So in the main query you can use order by.

08:25.390 --> 08:29.710
But in the CTE this is the only thing that you cannot use inside the city.

08:29.750 --> 08:30.590
So that's it.

08:30.590 --> 08:33.350
This is our first CTE in this section.

08:33.390 --> 08:33.790
All right.

08:33.790 --> 08:37.270
So this is the simplest form of the CTE the standalone.

08:37.550 --> 08:39.430
Now we can have not only one CTE.

08:39.470 --> 08:41.990
We can have multiple cities.
